{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-140189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066994/state.json" "file_sha256" "d46d37e4b5fc29dfdc41d921c01c53f0ee1472dab43dafbc6f43662a5f56083e"} {"question" "q-140189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066994/state.json" "file_sha256" "d46d37e4b5fc29dfdc41d921c01c53f0ee1472dab43dafbc6f43662a5f56083e"} {"question" "q-140189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e46cb2ea0664f07305e82609808ebbfd6440e117d12a2911ac18ad02f5cac21"} {"question" "q-140189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066994/state.json" "file_sha256" "d46d37e4b5fc29dfdc41d921c01c53f0ee1472dab43dafbc6f43662a5f56083e"} {"question" "q-140189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["m